msgid "Route authentication providers (accounts.google.com, login.microsoftonline.com, appleid.apple.com, …) — the whole domain family of every learned auth host (accounts.autodesk.com learned → all *.autodesk.com) — and the IP-bound login infrastructure (Clerk bot checks, hCaptcha, reCAPTCHA, Cloudflare Turnstile) through the SAME live exit the service itself uses. DNS goes through the encrypted pool and TCP is forced (QUIC and HTTPS/SVCB records are filtered). Fixes \"Sign in with Google\" loops on proxied services: every leg of the flow — page, provider, captcha, bot checks — rides one consistent exit instead of bouncing between countries and IPs."
msgstr ""

