msgid "Apply this strategy for %s: a SCOPED profile is built (other managed resources keep their strategies), the rule goes to Zapret, then the resource is checked live — page, CDN and the REAL video stream. Continue?"
msgstr ""

msgid "The global \"Apply strategy\" serves EVERY flow routed to Zapret (one engine strategy, no hostlists — the routing rules select the traffic). A per-resource apply (Strategy Lab rows, auto-pick) builds a SCOPED profile instead — other managed resources keep their strategies; the Composition below edits the same blocks manually. Applying also enables Zapret and restarts the service; testing runs the strategy on an isolated queue over 4 test sites (YouTube, Telegram, Discord, Speedtest)."
msgstr ""

msgid "The fuzzer batch-tests every strategy from the catalog on an isolated NFQUEUE (YouTube / Telegram / Discord / Speedtest TLS handshakes), then deep-checks the best strategy of EVERY technique family (multisplit, disorder, hostfakesplit, fakesplit, syndata, …), the best imported/generated strategies and your CURRENT strategy with REAL content fetches — measuring the fresh-connection start (the hover-preview latency, median of several fresh connections) and the sustained video flow in KB/s (a handshake cannot see TSPU throttling). The ranking: a >25% better start wins first, then a >10% better flow, then the handshake — a fast bulk with a slow start loses. Probes that all deep-tested strategies pass or fail identically do not rank (non-differential): the Resource loads column then shows ≈ with the raw pass count. A no-desync baseline marks hosts your ISP does not block; each host must pass the majority of rounds. Live traffic is untouched. A quick sweep takes ~15–30 minutes; a full one scales with the corpus (the label above computes it)."
msgstr ""

