msgid "• <b>Bypass blocking (rule lists)</b> — the everyday WORKING mode: everything stays direct, and traffic matching Routing Rules (YouTube, Russia Inside, Re-filter…) goes through the Main node — that is exactly what opens blocked sites without tunneling the whole connection. The bypass engines (Zapret / ByeDPI) and the Automation engine work here.<br>• <b>Everything through node</b> — ALL traffic goes through the Main node; per-service rules are not used.<br>• <b>Direct (all mechanisms off)</b> — for repairs and diagnostics: interception, engines, the DNS scheme and the core itself are OFF, the router just hands out the internet as the provider gives it.<br>Changing the mode re-renders the page so only relevant options stay visible"
