msgid "Checks a set of test services (YouTube, Discord, Telegram, WhatsApp, Google AI, OpenAI, Claude, Twitch…) through your real paths. The VERDICT speaks about your CONFIGURED routing (rules, learned lists and Zapret/ByeDPI desync) — the way LAN clients are actually served; the Direct column is reference: it shows whether the resource could open with no VPN at all. A response whose redirect chain is reset mid-way is not a success, and a 200 with an application-level refusal (geo, Gemini \"something went wrong\") is not either. When a refusal is about the remote region rather than the local provider, the verdict says so (geo-block) — a routing strategy cannot fix a region refusal, a node with a supported region can. RU services (rutube, gosuslugi) are control hosts — they must always open directly. The Cause line under the verdict explains WHY the resource fails (provider DPI, origin geo/WAF, DNS tampering, own rules) with a confidence level — hover it for the measured evidence."
