msgid "Always used while it responds — the engine leaves it only when it really dies (several dead probes in a row with a live reserve) and returns to it once it recovers. With \"Upgrade\" enabled the engine may also move to a node that stays faster by more than the tolerance for several probe rounds."
msgstr ""

msgid "Switch tolerance"
msgstr ""

msgid "Minimum latency gap (ms) required to move to a faster node — prevents flapping between nodes with close latency values. In \"Hold the preferred node\" mode it applies only when Upgrade is enabled."
msgstr ""

msgid "Preferred UDP node"
msgstr ""

msgid "For the separate UDP exit in \"Hold the preferred node\" mode: this node is held while it responds. Leave empty to use the main preferred node."
msgstr ""

msgid "Priority order of the failover reserves: add nodes in order, the topmost is tried first when the active pick dies. Reserves are probed live (this keeps their tunnels warm). Empty = every node may be used as a reserve. In URLTest modes only nodes of the pool are eligible; with a specific main node the main node itself is always first and cannot be removed."
msgstr ""

msgid "How often the active pick and the reserves are verified (seconds). Lower = faster failover (a dead main is usually replaced within ~10-20 s), higher = less background traffic."
msgstr ""

msgid "Return after recovery"
msgstr ""

msgid "When the held node recovers (or the preferred node is alive again), switch back after it stays stable for a while (3 good probes over 30+ seconds). Turn this off to stay on the failover node until it dies. The engine never overrides your manual pick while it stays alive."
msgstr ""

msgid "Upgrade on a better node"
msgstr ""

msgid "Only in \"Hold the preferred node\" mode: allow moving to a node that stays faster by more than the Switch tolerance for 3 probe rounds in a row (with a direct probe). Off by default — the preferred node is held regardless of latency."
msgstr ""

